  "details": "When I spawn in a world instance my frames lock to 60fps both in desktop and pcvr modes. Depending on the world, the fps lock occurs either when I am looking at a specific object or just the world in total, except the sky, when the frames return back to normal numbers while I am looking at it. I have checked that there is no fps limit on vrchat  or the anti-cheat software through my GPU software (AMD Software: Adrenaline Edition) and the fps limit inside vrchat I have set to 122fps on desktop and 90Hz in pcvr (with Quest 3). 3 months ago before summer it run normally but ever since I came back from holidays last week this issue has appeared. No issues appearing on any other vr or non-vr games, it's only happening in vrchat.",
